## 11. Physical interpretation

The GR and TPV descriptions may be summarized as

\[
\boxed{
\text{metric geometry}
\quad\longleftrightarrow\quad
\text{constitutive state of vacuum-spacetime}.
}
\tag{59}
\]

Likewise,

\[
\boxed{
\text{curvature}
\quad\longleftrightarrow\quad
\text{invariant nonuniformity of the constitutive state}.
}
\tag{60}
\]

and

\[
\boxed{
\text{gravitational radiation}
\quad\longleftrightarrow\quad
\text{propagating tensor constitutive deformation}.
}
\tag{61}
\]

The word “vacuum” does not denote empty space plus a material ingredient. It denotes the dynamical spacetime manifold itself.

The word “polarizable” denotes its constitutive response to the distribution and motion of matter and energy.

The word “tensor” emphasizes that its gravitational state cannot in general be represented by a scalar refractive index. A general spacetime requires tensorial spatial response, magnetoelectric structure in non-static foliations, and a dynamical volume element.

This interpretation is compatible with earlier constitutive approaches to spacetime while avoiding identification with a literal laboratory dielectric. Covariant formulations of constitutive electrodynamics show that permittivity, permeability and magnetoelectric tensors are observer-dependent pieces of a unified four-dimensional constitutive tensor.

