## 13. What TPV does not yet explain

Exact equivalence places sharp limits on the claims that may be made.

Baseline TPV does **not** explain why the Einstein-Hilbert action is selected from deeper microscopic principles.

It does not derive quantum gravity.

It does not derive Standard Model matter as excitations of the vacuum.

It does not resolve the cosmological constant problem.

It does not predict dark matter or dark energy beyond what the corresponding GR matter model predicts.

It does not provide a microscopic mechanical substrate analogous to atoms in an ordinary dielectric.

And, because it is exactly equivalent to GR,

\[
\text{baseline TPV cannot produce an observable deviation from GR}.
\tag{64}
\]

Those are separate research questions.

The present result is narrower but stronger: a tensor-polarizable-vacuum ontology can be formulated without contradicting general relativity because it can be made mathematically identical to general relativity.

