## 15. Discussion

The formal construction resolves several ambiguities that commonly arise in polarizable-vacuum descriptions.

First, TPV does not place a medium inside a background spacetime. The metric and constitutive state are the same physical object represented differently.

Second, polarization is tensorial and covariant. Coordinate permittivities and permeabilities are derived quantities rather than fundamental fields.

Third, electromagnetic constitutive information alone is insufficient to specify the full spacetime metric because of conformal invariance in four dimensions. Including the metric volume form removes this degeneracy.

Fourth, no extra dynamical field has been introduced. Hence the GR Hamiltonian constraints and two tensor degrees of freedom survive exactly.

Fifth, matter continues to couple universally to a single physical metric. Consequently geodesic structure, causal cones and stress-energy conservation are untouched.

Finally, the interpretation is compatible with the broader observation that Einstein dynamics can itself be encoded in constitutive variables. Recent work extending the Plebanski mapping to ADM dynamics provides an explicit field-equation-level realization in which lapse, shift, spatial metric, extrinsic curvature and tensor gravitational waves can be represented through corresponding constitutive quantities.

The distinction is that TPV does not treat such a medium as an engineered analogue. It interprets the constitutive variables as a representation of the physical spacetime itself.

---

## 16. Conclusion

We have constructed an exactly general-relativistic Tensor Polarizable Vacuum interpretation.

The fundamental dictionary is

\[
\boxed{
g_{\mu\nu}
\;\longleftrightarrow\;
\mathcal C
=
\left(
\star_g|_{\Lambda^2},
\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_g
\right).
}
\tag{67}
\]

The constitutive Hodge operator fixes the conformal spacetime geometry and the volume form fixes the remaining conformal scale. The map is therefore invertible.

Defining

\[
S_{\rm TPV}[\mathcal C,\Psi]
=
S_{\rm GR}[g[\mathcal C],\Psi]
\tag{68}
\]

gives a theory whose equations of motion, constraint algebra, matter conservation, causal structure, gravitational degrees of freedom and observables are precisely those of general relativity.

Accordingly,

\[
\boxed{
\mathrm{TPV}_{\rm GR}
\equiv
\mathrm{GR}
}
\tag{69}
\]

as a classical physical theory.

The distinction is interpretive:

\[
\boxed{
\text{spacetime is the tensor-polarizable vacuum}.
}
\tag{70}
\]

What general relativity calls the metric is the constitutive state of that vacuum-spacetime; what GR calls curvature is the invariant geometric structure of its polarization; and what GR calls gravitational radiation is propagating tensor deformation of that same constitutive state.

No additional medium is required.

No preferred background is required.

No additional gravitational degree of freedom is required.

No departure from general relativity is predicted.

This establishes Tensor Polarizable Vacuum as a mathematically viable constitutive interpretation of general relativity and supplies a sharply defined GR limit for future physically active TPV extensions.

